    "Title": "Multi-target prediction based on ChEMBL data",
    "Description": "Estimates which of 616 protein targets a compound is likely to bind, using the multitask model developed by the ChEMBL team from curated compound-target pairs. Activity thresholds were set per protein family rather than uniformly, reflecting that a meaningful potency cut-off differs between kinases, GPCRs and ion channels. Coverage mirrors the ChEMBL literature, so heavily studied targets are well represented while many proteins of interest are absent entirely.",
